ally are but how damaging is green  washing well the outgoing chair of the  environment agency emma howard boyd says  businesses need to be transparent about  their net zero plans because otherwise  it's creating a full sense of confidence  about how the climate crisis is being  tackled  ecargo bikes and a team of on-foot  delivery staff are set to replace  thousands of amazon delivery vans in  london amazon will open its first micro  mobility hub in hackney in east london  as part of its efforts to cut its carbon  emissions the online retailer plans to  deliver half of its uk shipments with  net zero carbon by 2030 and all by 2040  now take a look at this world  record-breaking water lily it was grown  at kew gardens in london and it's got  scientists excited because it's been  revealed as a species new to science the  famous water lily has grown at the  botanic gardens for 177 years and it's  the first discovery of a new giant water  lily in over a century researchers on  the project have called the discovery  fundamentally important in the face of  fast  biodiversity loss  and before we go we want your climate  questions anything that's ever mystified  you or whatever you want to get to the  bottom of if you scan the qr code on  your screen right now you can send us  your questions some of which will be  answered on our new weekend climate show  hosted by the environment broadcaster  and author tom heap and you'll be able  to watch that on saturday and on sunday  at 3 30 here on sky news  well that's all from us for now thanks  for watching and we'll see you next time  bye  [Music]
 

